1. WHAT THIS PROJECT IS
-----------------------

An independent, educational reimplementation of the method described in:

  S. Godbole, A. Kattukaran, S. Savla, V. Pradhan, P. Kanani and D. Patil,
  "Enhancing Paediatric Pneumonia Detection and Classification Using
  Customized CNNs and Transfer Learning Based Ensemble Models",
  Int. Res. J. Multidisc. Technovation, vol. 6, no. 6, pp. 38-53, 2024.
  doi: 10.54392/irjtmt2463

The code here was written from the paper's published description. It is not the
authors' code, it is not affiliated with or endorsed by them, and the results
obtained with it differ materially from the paper's reported results (see
docs/RESULTS.md). Any error in the reimplementation is ours, not theirs.


2. EDUCATIONAL USE ONLY — NOT A MEDICAL DEVICE
----------------------------------------------

This software is provided for teaching, research and portfolio work.

  * It is NOT a medical device.
  * It is NOT cleared or approved by any regulatory authority (FDA, CE, or
    otherwise).
  * It MUST NOT be used to diagnose, triage, screen or otherwise influence the
    care of any patient.
  * It MUST NOT be presented in clinical, commercial or patient-facing material
    without independent regulatory review.
  * Reported probabilities are outputs of a class-weighted classifier at a
    fixed decision threshold. They are not calibrated clinical risks.

The training data covers paediatric patients aged 1-5 from a single
institution, and the model recognises exactly two pneumonia subtypes. Any other
pathology, adult patient, or out-of-distribution image will be misclassified.

The authors of this repository accept no liability for any use outside the
scope described above.


